// Collision Colors renderer-path diagnostic for retail SCUS_974.65.
//
// This does not use the injected ELF, does not hook 0x00139A48, and does not
// call libdl/game helpers. It only forces terrain-fragment vertex colors inside
// LightTfrags to 0xffffffff so we can verify that renderer-side coloring is a
// viable path without freezing the game.
//
// Test this file by itself. Do not also enable bin/collision-colors.bin.pnach.
//
// Important: these addresses are based on ProjectRYNO retail symbols:
//   LightTfrags = 0x004e4000
// The earlier 0x00591xxx diagnostic came from a loaded Sarathos map memory
// image in Ghidra and can freeze when used as a PNACH against the retail ELF.

// LightTfrags first packed-color path:
patch=1,EE,204E4278,extended,2401FFFF // addiu at, zero, -1
patch=1,EE,204E4280,extended,2402FFFF // addiu v0, zero, -1

// LightTfrags single-color path:
patch=1,EE,204E4450,extended,2401FFFF // addiu at, zero, -1

// LightTfrags alternate color path:
patch=1,EE,204E4634,extended,2402FFFF // addiu v0, zero, -1
